      "dom_id": "step-q171905",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14201070/assets/bd6b42e1d48ca0e45ffc9b8910345bea52f1f44f9754f00ac4a4ba034e273bb5.png)\n\nGiven the quadrilateral above, we have $x=${{field-1}}\n${}^{∘}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+3x+(2x+{20}^{∘})+(5x-{24}^{∘}) & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 14x-{4}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 14x & ={364}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={26}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
