    "q-223201": {
      "dom_id": "step-q223201",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14201070/assets/33c1016cb2353e5332a5e04e8f377d4fa7d76e1b569a3532a45c5a068cc6d255.png)\n\nFor the quadrilateral above, determine the measure of the exterior angle of $∠C.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6x+{23}^{∘})+(17x-{4}^{∘})+(21x+{8}^{∘})+(4x-{3}^{∘}) & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 48x+{24}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 48x & ={336}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={7}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of the exterior angle of $∠C$ equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}21x+{8}^{∘} & =21({7}^{∘})+{8}^{∘} \\\\  & ={147}^{∘}+8 \\\\  & ={155}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
