    "q-223356": {
      "dom_id": "step-q223356",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14201070/assets/9e40dfd3842ec7a7b5de16d7938988e86209960ae9cba510bbac004b0bb73d94.png)\n\nFor the pentagon above, the measure of the exterior angle of $∠B$ is{{field-1}}\n${}^{∘}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let us call $x$ the exterior angle of $∠B.$ Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{58}^{∘}+x+{65}^{∘}+{63}^{∘}+{97}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ x+{283}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={77}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
